A||||4||Andre||Getrag from late model Sunfire GT||||5||
Z||000000||Andre||02-14-2001||08:51 PM||||Does anybody have the specifications for the latest Getrag Transaxles from the 2000 model year Sunfire GT and Cavalier Z24:  Torgue Rating, Gear Ratios and Final Drive Ratio.<P>I assume these boxes are a direct bolt-on to the 3.8, 3.8SC and Northstar.  I'm not concerned about any frame mounting details.||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||02-14-2001||10:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Andre:<BR><B>Does anybody have the specifications for the latest Getrag Transaxles from the 2000 model year Sunfire GT and Cavalier Z24:  Torgue Rating, Gear Ratios and Final Drive Ratio.<P>I assume these boxes are a direct bolt-on to the 3.8, 3.8SC and Northstar.  I'm not concerned about any frame mounting details.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I believe you are assuming wrong.  I have an Isuzu 5 speed from a 97 Sunfire and it has the Quad 4 bell housing bolt pattern.  I believe that they would not change the engine bell housing to mate with the transaxle so I believe the new Getrag will probably have the same bolt pattern as the earlier Isuzu and that means the Quad 4.<P>The Quad 4/TwinCam bell housing bolt pattern is <B>NOT</B> like anyother GM product.<P>Paul<BR><P>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com||||reg||9
Z||000002||Will||02-15-2001||10:17 AM||||As I understand it, the bolt pattern is the same, but the starter location is different. A sunfire Getrag could be used with a Northstar because the N* starter is inside the belel housing directly above the crankshaft centerline, and needs to have the bell housing modified anyway.<BR>I'm sure it could be done, but you may have to cut and weld on the bell housing. That's not that a big deal; it's cast aluminum.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Andre||02-15-2001||01:21 PM||||Thanks Will for confirming that the Sunfire Getrag can be used with the N*.  I'm planning a N* conversion on my '88 GT, and try to establish which 5-spd to use:<BR>1. Current Getrag 282 ~ 200 ft-lb, 3.61 final drive.<BR>2. Getrag 284 ~ 250 ft-lb, same ratios.<BR>3. New Sunfire Getrag ~ ??? ft-lb, ??? final drive ratio.<P>The new Sunfire Getrag is very attractive since it's a newer design, and the linkages are far superior to the original Fiero linkages.<P>BUT, I don't have the Torgue Rating and Gear Ratios of the new transaxle - ANYBODY that can help?||||reg||3
Z||000004||Will||02-15-2001||03:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Andre:<BR><B>Thanks Will for confirming that the Sunfire Getrag can be used with the N*.  I'm planning a N* conversion on my '88 GT, and try to establish which 5-spd to use:<BR>1. Current Getrag 282 ~ 200 ft-lb, 3.61 final drive.<BR>2. Getrag 284 ~ 250 ft-lb, same ratios.<BR>3. New Sunfire Getrag ~ ??? ft-lb, ??? final drive ratio.<P>The new Sunfire Getrag is very attractive since it's a newer design, and the linkages are far superior to the original Fiero linkages.<P>BUT, I don't have the Torgue Rating and Gear Ratios of the new transaxle - ANYBODY that can help?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'd guess that the torque rating and internal construction (including gear ratios) have not changed significantly, except for the final drive ratio, which is 3.94 in a Quad 4 transmission.<P>You do NOT want the 284. If you break it, it will be MUCHO DINERO to replace. It can not be repaired anywhere but at the factory, and even has "do not disassemble" stamped on the case.<P>I guess you mean external shift linkages? how are they superior? I've never seen one really close.||||reg||1
